================================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the work authored for this project:

  Geography/src/geography/**       the agent-based model (Java)
  scripts/**                       data acquisition, analysis, scenario
                                   construction, figure generation, validation
  docs/**                          documentation written for this project,
                                   EXCEPT the third-party items listed below
  Geography/batch/**               run configuration files
  Geography/data/registry/**       the variable and assumption registries
  Geography/data/shelters/*.csv    the shelter inventory compiled for this
                                   project from the public sources named in
                                   Geography/data/README.md

It does NOT cover the following, each of which carries its own terms. Nothing
here grants you any right to any of them.


1. REPAST SIMPHONY AND ITS DEPENDENCIES
   Geography/repast-licenses/     (41 dependency license texts)
   (The inherited stock-demo data and Geography/license.txt were removed in the
   v1.0 cleanup -- loaded by no code path, and that license.txt contradicted
   this file. Both remain recoverable from git history.)

   Repast Simphony is distributed under its own terms; see
   Geography/repast-licenses/repast-license.txt. GeographicLib, the JTS
   Topology Suite and GeoTools likewise carry their own licenses, included in
   that directory.


2. THE SPRINGER CHAPTER CLASS
   docs/chapter/svmult.cls
   docs/publication/template/OFFICIAL-template/**

   Copyright Springer-Verlag. Redistributed here only as supplied with the
   2026 Summer Proceedings chapter template, for the purpose of compiling this
   chapter. Not relicensed.


3. THE STREET CENTERLINE DATA  --  REDISTRIBUTED WITH THE PROVIDER'S APPROVAL
   Geography/data/Streets.shp, .dbf, .shx, .prj, .cpg
   Streets.zip

   Street centerlines from the Regional Land Information System (RLIS),
   Oregon Metro (inferred from the attribute schema). Please credit the source
   as: Regional Land Information System (RLIS), Oregon Metro.

   Redistribution of the RLIS-derived products in this repository is with the
   provider's approval, recorded as follows and no more strongly: THE
   RESEARCHER REPORTS THAT OREGON METRO APPROVED THE REDISTRIBUTION (relayed
   2026-08-02). No written determination from Oregon Metro is on file anywhere
   in this repository; the record of the approval is the researcher's report
   of it. No reference number, contact name, approval date, license name,
   license version, or license URL is asserted here, because none has been
   recorded.

   A separate provenance gap remains and is NOT closed by that approval: this
   file was supplied with the inherited project and predates version control
   here, so its original download date and RLIS release version could not be
   recovered. That gap is documented in Geography/data/README.md and
   docs/science/DATA_SOURCES.md (source D0), and is stated in the published
   chapter. If you need a citable release version, obtain the layer directly
   from Metro / gis-pdx.opendata.arcgis.com under their terms rather than
   relying on the copy here.


4. PUBLIC-SECTOR DATA (redistributed, not owned)
   Geography/data/airnow/aqs_hourly_pm25_portland_2020-09.csv
       U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, Air Quality System. A work of the
       U.S. federal government and therefore in the public domain. EPA asks
       that AQS be acknowledged as the source.

   Geography/data/encampments/irp_campsite_reports_sample.csv
       City of Portland (Impact Reduction Program campsite reports, obtained
       from the City's open-data ArcGIS service). Please credit the source as:
       City of Portland, Impact Reduction Program campsite reports.

       The campsite-report-derived products in this repository are
       redistributed with the provider's approval, recorded as follows and no
       more strongly: THE RESEARCHER REPORTS THAT THE CITY OF PORTLAND
       APPROVED THE REDISTRIBUTION (relayed 2026-08-02). No written
       determination from the City is on file anywhere in this repository; the
       record of the approval is the researcher's report of it. No reference
       number, contact name, approval date, license name, license version, or
       license URL is asserted here, because none has been recorded.

   Both are reproducible from their original sources by the fetch scripts in
   scripts/, and every file carries a SHA-256 checksum in
   Geography/data/README.md.


5. THIRD-PARTY DOCUMENTS INCLUDED FOR REFERENCE
   docs/publication/template/EXAMPLE-chapter-VanPelt-2026.pdf
